From b6fe81d5ddc8a946f9222ebf92ce3fd1d89112bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 07:23:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: rebrand, retire modules/[skill] roster, fix Reports
 exclusivity bug, rename Capabilities, rework Library terminology
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Branding

layout.tsx's metadata still said title: "mudd 1.34", description:
"Showtime Revenue Infrastructure Panel" (also product-specific, wrong
direction for a unified interface) — renamed to "Unified Tools Platform"
and a generic description; added the new favicon (logos/homelg.png).
The pre-login landing page's header still showed the old logo.png under
alt="Mudd Ventures" — replaced with the same new asset. Left "©
Mudd Ventures 2026" in that same footer untouched — that could be a real
legal entity name distinct from the product's own branding, not
something to guess-rename.

## modules/[skill] retired

Used to render ModuleClientRoster — a roster of every client with a
given skill enabled, plus (for 5 Showtime skills) an "Activity" tab
showing a run-execution log with cancel/retry/dismiss actions. One
workspace = one client made the roster a list of exactly one, and the
run-log-with-actions it hid behind a tab click turned out to be the
exact same thing the engagement page's own Run History section already
provides (same cancel/retry/dismiss, via run-row-actions.tsx) — just
always visible there instead of needing a second page. Now a redirect
into that: the one client's engagement page, run history pre-filtered
to the skill via its own `?skill=` param, scrolled to a new
id="run-history" anchor.

New workerPrimaryHref() (worker-registry.ts) is the one place that
decides where a worker's real single-client page lives — its own
schedule/report page (4 Showtime skills), RM's shared findings page (5
RM skills), or the engagement page's filtered Run History (pin-down,
rep-onboarding, which have neither). WorkersPanel's Pipeline/Findings
links and Capabilities' own links both now read from this one function
instead of independently hardcoding the same two arrays.

## Capabilities → Installed Skills, rebuilt as real actions

Renamed, and rebuilt from a static read-only icon grid (whose only
action was linking to the roster just retired above) into working rows:
a real on/off toggle (the same enable/disable endpoint WorkersPanel's
own toggle calls), a Configure icon, and a View icon — the toggle/
configure/view shape already established elsewhere (AutopilotTable),
adapted to what a 240px sidebar can actually hold. Configure and View
are real navigations, not inline forms — the five config forms need
real width (multi-column layouts, a template-picker grid) a sidebar
this narrow structurally can't provide, the same conclusion already
reached for this exact grid before this pass. Deliberately not a second
place to enable a new skill — turning one off here just drops it from
this "what's on" list; Library stays the one place a skill gets turned
on in the first place.

## Reports: fixed a real exclusivity bug, dropped dead multi-client plumbing

`!repIdentityGraphRow && selected.bookingPlatform` gated Showtime's
report card off entirely whenever an RM identity graph existed — a
client running both products only ever saw the RM card. The engagement
page's own report section already renders both cards independently
when both apply; Reports hadn't matched that. Also dropped
listReportableClients/`?client=`/`?product=` — machinery for a client
picker (reports-sidebar-section.tsx's "Client Reports" list) that's
been unrouted since the secondary-sidebar collapse, silently falling
through to clients[0] and only "working" because there's now genuinely
one client to fall through to. Replaced with resolving that one client
directly.

## Library terminology: "worker" (internal) vs "skill" (what a user reads)

User-facing copy only — WorkerId/WorkerDefinition/WORKER_REGISTRY etc.
stay as internal implementation names throughout, never shown to a
user. Library's heading, counts, search placeholder, and empty states
now say "skill(s)" instead of "worker(s)"; Enable/Enabled/Enabling
became Install/Installed/Installing (Library's card, its error
messages, and the Pile-On quick-setup modal's title/button/chat
message) — directly answering "I don't even know where to install
anymore": that action always silently installed the underlying product
before turning the skill on, it just wasn't labeled as installing
anything. WorkersPanel's own heading changed from "Workers" to
"Skills" with copy now saying explicitly that Showtime and Reputation
Manager skills render in the same list together, confirming (not just
by inspection) what workerIds already merges: enabling Reputation
Manager for this client does make its skills appear in this same
panel, right alongside Showtime's — verified true via engagements/[id]/
page.tsx's own construction of that list, not assumed.

## Also fixed while in the area

WorkersPanel's per-card action row never linked to that worker's own
Phase 8 analytics page — Library's worker-card.tsx always has; added
the same Analytics link here so it's not the one place a worker's real
run stats were unreachable from.

## Verified clean

tsc: only the 5 pre-existing baseline errors. eslint: clean (2
pre-existing <img> warnings on landing-wrapper.tsx, unrelated to this
change — that file already used plain <img> before this pass). Full
production build passes.

## Found but not touched — flagged, not fixed

- reports-sidebar.tsx, reports-sidebar-section.tsx, reports-client-
  links.tsx are now fully dead (zero live importers) — left in place,
  not deleted, same as every other dead-file call this restructure has
  made.
- src/components/master-client-roster.tsx duplicate-exports
  ModuleClientRoster under the same name as module-client-roster.tsx —
  an orphaned leftover file, unrelated to this pass, nothing imports it.
- "© Mudd Ventures 2026" in the landing page footer — see Branding
  above, a real question rather than a silent guess.

